From c3ae94986181e42713187422f8988df22c1c986c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:22:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Video: optics, portrait lip sync, and end frames
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three engine-level gaps, all opt-in and all no-ops when unused.

Cinematography
  lib/videoGen/cinematography.ts: which camera body, lens, focal length
  and aperture a shot is "shot on". Motion presets (patch 1) say how the
  camera MOVES; this says what the camera IS, and the two are
  independent — a dolly-in on 16mm at f/1.4 is a different shot from the
  same move on an 8K digital body at f/11, and changing one must not
  disturb the other. Every axis is independently optional, because
  "shallow depth of field, I don't care what body" is a real request.

  Applied per job across every AI engine, and normalized on the way in:
  a job's options are replayed on every retry, so an option removed from
  the catalog later degrades to "not set" rather than breaking a render
  months from now.

Lip sync: portraits and your own voice
  Two things were missing around a feature pinned to one model:

  - BRING YOUR OWN AUDIO, on both modes and needing no configuration.
    Upload a voice note, a podcast clip, an actor's take, and it speaks
    instead of the synthesiser. Synthesising stays the default; the
    script is simply no longer mandatory when a recording is attached,
    and preflight stops demanding a TTS provider for a job that will
    never call one.
  - PORTRAIT mode: one headshot plus audio becomes a talking video, so a
    founder gets a spokesperson without ever standing in front of a
    camera.

  Portrait mode needs a model that takes an IMAGE plus audio, and this
  repo pins none — so rather than ship a guessed Replicate slug and
  version hash that would 404 on the first paid job, the portrait model
  is admin-configured (video_gen_settings.lip_sync_portrait_model) and
  preflight refuses portrait jobs with the one thing an admin has to do.
  Video-mode lip sync (LatentSync) is unchanged and needs nothing.

  The consent hard gate applies to portraits exactly as it does to
  video — it matters more for a photo, not less.

End frames
  image_to_video takes an optional SECOND photo as the last frame:
  "start here, end there", which is what makes a product reveal or a
  before/after transition possible. Before this, sourceImagePaths
  accepted twenty photos and animated the first.

  Gated on a catalog capability (supportsEndFrame), so a model that
  cannot blend two stills is a 400 before funding rather than a silently
  discarded photo. And because hosted model schemas move under us, a
  model that rejects the request WITH an end frame is retried once
  without it: the user still gets the video they paid for, degraded to a
  plain animation, instead of losing the job over an optional extra.

Deliberately NOT in this patch, with reasons:
  - Continue/extend an existing render. Seedance 2.0 Extend continues a
    generation by its request_id, but neither Replicate nor OpenRouter's
    video API exposes that handle to us, so there is nothing to build
    against today. It needs a provider that returns and accepts a
    continuation id.
  - Multi-reference subject consistency (images_list) and the v2v
    watermark remover. Both need a specific model whose input schema I
    cannot verify from here; guessing a slug would cost a paid job.
    Character lock already covers the people case.

Migration: one additive nullable column
(video_gen_settings.lip_sync_portrait_model) plus optional JSON fields
on existing options — pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push.

Verified: pnpm run typecheck clean; api-server 2280/2281 (the one
failure, ads.meta-reconnect, fails identically on 8138eab without a Meta
app credential in env); web 838/838; spec lints, codegen drift clean.

